   "2026-10-23-moridinamael-ddcb5510",
   "The chunk \"ass\" when the tokenizer cuts it off as its own piece: after a hyphen in compounds (Steam-Assisted, Quality-Assurance, power-assisted, self-assessment, lane-assist, character-assassination), at the start of names like Assam and Assassin's Creed, and the standalone word for a donkey. Quiet for ordinary whole words that merely contain the letters (assist, assess, assets, assignment, Assembly, class, glass, embassy, Massachusetts, unhyphenated \"Quality Assurance\") and for hyphen splits that give \"-as\" (machine-assembled). Weak (about 0.3-0.4) on short words ending in -ass (grass, bass, brass).",
